--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 75e7bea227aaf2b499307efe1ddc0480, type: 3}
  m_Name: CurioDialog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCDialog
  NPCName: Curio
  DialogLines:
  - text: "Chief\u2026 you may have noticed the district feels\u2026 disorganized."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: Before the storm, the city kept quiet notes about what each traveler enjoyed.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: It used those notes to guide people toward places they would probably like.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: Puzzle halls for thinkers. Arenas for fighters. Markets for collectors.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: "Those notes were lost when the town\u2019s memory fractured..."
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: If you approve, I can begin rebuilding that system.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: But it would mean keeping a small preference card for each visitor...
    isQuestion: 1
    choices:
    - choiceText: Rebuild the guidance system.
      nextDialogIndex: 7
    - choiceText: Let travelers explore freely.
      nextDialogIndex: 8
  - text: Understood. The city will begin remembering what interests its visitors.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
  - text: Very well. Sometimes discovery is better without guidance.
    isQuestion: 0
    choices: []
